Where Snowball takes its vocabulary from another source, as a dump of
Wikipedia (CC BY-SA), the Wortschatz Leipzig corpus, the srWaC corpus, a
spelling dictionary or a GPL word list, the sample keeps about 100 words,
a short list of words and their stems, kept as test data alone. These are
arabic, armenian, basque, catalan, czech, esperanto, estonian, finnish,
french, greek, hindi, indonesian, italian, lithuanian, persian, polish,
serbian, sesotho, tamil, ukrainian and yiddish. Each source is named in
snowball-data's COPYING of that language.
